# MaiRide runtime and release guards

## Protected auth runtime

Never modify, replace, or refactor these files unless the user explicitly asks:

- `src/lib/supabase.ts`
- `api/_lib/supabaseRuntime.ts`

Do not rewrite their auth/session wiring, env loading, or client factories as part of unrelated work.

## Demo account isolation

Preserve `is_demo` JSON payload isolation for demo accounts.

- Demo responses must keep `is_demo` (or equivalent demo markers) intact.
- Do not mix demo payloads into live/production account flows.
- Do not strip, rename, or bypass demo isolation when changing APIs, booking, payments, or user data paths.

## WebKit / Safari UI

When changing UI (layout, CSS, motion, forms, maps, modals):

- Prefer CSS that works in Safari / WebKit (avoid unsupported features without fallbacks).
- Watch for flex/grid overflow, `100vh`/`dvh`, backdrop-filter, sticky, and date/input quirks.
- Verify mobile Safari behavior for interactive surfaces before considering UI done.

## Build verification

After major edits (multi-file changes, routing, API handlers, auth-adjacent work, or release packaging):

```bash
npm run build
```

Fix any syntax/type/build errors before finishing. Do not leave the tree in a non-building state.
